## Overview
Layered design with strict dependency direction, centralized communication policies, and a command pattern. Public API is static and self-initializing.

## Layers and Dependency Direction
- Workflow/Orchestration → State/Primitives → Native Wrapper
- Allowed: `SmartPrintManager` → `ZebraPrinterManager` → `ZebraPrinter`
- Forbidden: upward references or circular imports

Mermaid diagram:
```mermaid
graph TD
  UI[UI / Static API (Zebra)] --> SPM[SmartPrintManager]
  SPM --> ZPM[ZebraPrinterManager]
  ZPM --> ZP[ZebraPrinter]
  ZP --> Native[ZSDK (iOS) / Platform]
```

## Core Components (with references)
- Zebra (static API): Single entry point; auto-initialization; exposes discovery, connection, print, status
  - See: `lib/zebra.dart`
- SmartPrintManager: Orchestrates workflows (retries, events, progress, error handling)
  - See: `lib/smart_print_manager.dart`
- ZebraPrinterManager: Manages printer instances, connection state, primitive ops
  - See: `lib/zebra_printer_manager.dart`
- ZebraPrinter: Typed bridge to native layer; no workflow logic
  - See: `lib/zebra_printer.dart` and Native standards
- CommunicationPolicy: Connection assurance, retries, timeouts
  - See rule: communication policy (what to retry, when, and how)
  - File: `lib/internal/communication_policy.dart`
- Command Pattern: CommandFactory + BaseCommand + specific commands
  - See rules: command implementation/usage
  - Files: `lib/internal/commands/`
- Result Architecture: Central error/success codes and bridge
  - See rule: result and error-handling architecture
  - Files: `lib/models/result.dart`, `lib/internal/zebra_error_bridge.dart`

## Operation Types
- Simple: Single request/response (connect, print, getSetting)
- Streaming: Multiple events then complete (discovery, evented workflows)

Mermaid diagram:
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant Caller
  participant Zebra
  participant Policy as CommunicationPolicy
  participant Cmd as Command
  participant ZP as ZebraPrinter
  participant Native
  Caller->>Zebra: method(...)
  Zebra->>Policy: executeWithAssurance(fn)
  Policy->>Cmd: create/execute
  Cmd->>ZP: send/receive
  ZP->>Native: method channel / ZSDK
  Native-->>ZP: response/events
  ZP-->>Cmd: data
  Cmd-->>Policy: Result<T>
  Policy-->>Zebra: Result<T>
  Zebra-->>Caller: Result<T> / Stream<Event>
```

## Communication and Command Flow
- CommunicationPolicy wraps all hardware communication with retries and timeouts
- Commands are created via CommandFactory and executed through the policy
- Streaming operations forward events before completion
- Reference rules:
  - Communication policy (how assurance works)
  - Command implementation/usage (how to add and execute commands)

## Readiness Architecture
- PrinterReadiness lazily reads and caches per-property status; single hardware read per property
- PrinterReadinessManager uses cached values to apply fixes; does not re-read post-fix
- Options drive which properties are read and which fixes may run
- Reference rule: readiness architecture in `lib/models/printer_readiness.dart` and `lib/zebra_printer_readiness_manager.dart`

## Error Handling and Results
- All operations return `Result<T>`; no throws from library code
- ZebraErrorBridge maps ZSDK/native errors to centralized `ErrorCodes`
- Reference rule: result and error-handling architecture

## Native Layer Responsibilities
- Native is a thin bridge; no workflow or business logic
- iOS uses `ZSDKWrapper` with Swift binder in `ZebraPrinterInstance`
- Reference rule: native layer standards; iOS integration guide

## Best Practices
- Use static API for simplicity; managers for workflows
- Respect dependency direction; keep layers pure
- Prefer commands for hardware ops; never mix utility parsing with command strings
- Cache and reuse readiness values; reset only when justified

## Enforcement
- Violations of dependency direction and layering are not allowed
- Follow command, communication policy, and result/bridge rules
- Keep docs and code synchronized; update rules with changes

